{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You covered the mountains</b> — and the meaning of אל מקום is that which he mentioned after it — <b>boundary</b>. He mentioned בל ישובון — as a sign, for at first the earth was covered with waters, and by the will of HaShem, the wind pressed against the waters and the dry land appeared, after the light was created, which was the essence, as I explained in the account of Genesis."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {0 "The bracketed editorial heading is preserved as translated; the dash sequence in the source appears to mark a parenthetical reference to a subsequent word in the verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:12.098052564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}